---
title: "object_creation (Sui Move Concepts: Object Model)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_validate_key: check struct has key ability
    q_validate_key --> q_check_uid: has key ability
    q_validate_key --> q_abort: missing key ability
    q_check_uid --> q_new_uid: first field is id UID
    q_check_uid --> q_abort: first field is not id UID
    q_new_uid --> q_assign_uid: uid = object::new(ctx)
    q_assign_uid --> q_construct: Object { id: uid, ... }
    q_construct --> [*]: return object

    q_abort --> [*]: abort - bytecode verification failed

    note right of q_check_uid
        INV-001: Structs with key ability must have id UID as first field
        INV-002: UIDs are globally unique and never reused
    end note

    note right of q_new_uid
        INV-003: object::new(ctx) always produces a fresh UID
        INV-004: Bytecode verifier enforces new objects get fresh UIDs
    end note
